 "issue_body": "`spot=|f|\u00b70.001`, `transverse=|f|\u00b70.002` \u2014 no aperture/aberration dependence.\n   Thin model at `:103` also drops the thick term it cites at `:97`\n   (~1.7% error at R=\u00b150,d=5).",
 "issue_url": "https://github.com/pmaasz/openLens/issues/251",
 "pr": 269,
 "pr_title": "fix(chromatic): ray-traced spots and thick lensmaker in chromatic ana\u2026",
 "pr_body": "\u2026lysis\r\n\r\nReplace the fabricated spot/transverse estimates (|f|*0.001/0.002) with RMS/geometric spot radii from exact hexapolar ray traces per wavelength, and the thin focal model with the thick lensmaker equation (shared helper mirroring Lens.calculate_focal_length; thin dropped 1.7%). Lateral color is now the traced chief-ray centroid split at a documented 5-degree reference field instead of a difference of placeholders. Afocal geometries raise ValueError. Add regression tests (thick-f match, aperture scaling, f/V axial order, afocal).",
